{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":982454,"duration_api_ms":1052374,"num_turns":91,"result":"All tasks complete. Here is the execution payload:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Upgraded all four source-water presets to carry differentiated carbonate-relevant inputs (DIC and alkalinity) that produce meaningfully different equilibrium pH values under the carbonate solver. hard_shrimp: KH 8, DIC 35.7 mg C/L, Alk 2.856 meq/L → pH ~7.72. moderate: KH 4, DIC 19.4 mg C/L, Alk 1.428 meq/L → pH ~7.23. soft_acidic: KH 2, DIC 12.1 mg C/L, Alk 0.714 meq/L → pH ~6.75. ro_like: KH 0.1, DIC 1.2 mg C/L, Alk 0.036 meq/L → pH ~6.11 (was all-zero with neutral fallback pH 7.0). Updated provenance notes in each TOML with plain-language descriptions of what each profile emulates, including equilibrium pH range and buffering character. Added 8 tests covering DIC presence, alkalinity ordering, water-change dilution math for DIC and alkalinity, pH differentiation (>0.5 pH gap between soft and hard), RO buffering reduction, validation rejection of negative/NaN inputs, and a 500-hour integration test comparing soft vs hard tanks under feeding.\",\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    \"Pre-existing test failure: happy_plants_grow_with_light_and_nutrients in end_to_end.rs was already failing before this change (confirmed via git stash test on clean HEAD). Not caused by this task.\",\n    \"e2e baseline scenario envelope tests in tank_harness may need tightening in task 6e5.4.6 (Add carbonate regression tests) since source water chemistry has shifted. Current wide envelope bounds (pH 5.0-9.0) still pass.\",\n    \"The ro_like profile is no longer all-zeros. Tests that construct SourceWaterProfile::zero() directly (e.g. water_change_mass_balance) are unaffected, but any code that assumed the ro_like TOML preset had zero DIC/alkalinity would see different behavior.\"\n  ],\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Updated hard_shrimp.toml: DIC 22→35.7, Alk